From 0ab1df555d3eebc79c37b46a8d7768df438eed29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:15:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Fog light shafts at full resolution at every
 hdFogResolution (I-440)

- Half/quarter: the fog is marched at the low resolution as two brackets
  without shadow reads (shadowed layers all lit / all in shadow); the
  sun's share of the shadow-dependent light is marched per screen pixel
  (R32UI, half floats share + view depth), blurred depth-aware, and the
  composite blends the upsampled brackets by it
- Bracket upsample: 4x4 depth-weighted, then 8x8, then nearest depth (a
  plain blend put leaf fog on sky between leaves)
- Full resolution keeps the exact march and its two blurs unchanged
- gen_fog_spv.py: FOG_PASS 0..7

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJUrF3iBGsBKdyGrJjf
